          "why_it_matters": "Four nights at 9:30 Club turns a catalog-heavy rock show into something closer to a small residency. The current eight-piece setup adds three horns, each opening set centers a different album, and the second halves are built to vary while pulling from four decades of deliberately odd pop craft and new 2026 material. In the 40th-anniversary year of the self-titled debut, the value is not nostalgia alone: it is hearing a band that still treats arrangement, timbre, humor and structural left turns as part of the live language.",
